@startuml data_manager
!include style.iuml
title <size:20><b>data_manager – UML Class Diagram</b></size>\n<size:12>JSON storage · JSON Derulo · INF1103 Phase 2</size>

class RecordRepository {
  <i>stores ErrorLogs in processed_records.json</i>
  - _data_file : str
  - _records : ErrorLog [0..*]
  ==
  + __init__(data_file : str)
  + load_all() : ErrorLog [0..*]
  + save(log : ErrorLog) : bool
  + get(log_id : str) : ErrorLog | None
  + query(predicate : Callable[[ErrorLog], bool]) : ErrorLog [0..*]
  - _read_file() : dict [0..*]
  - _write_file(items : dict [0..*]) : bool
}

class ErrorLog <<logic_manager>> #F4F4F4 ##[dashed]888888

RecordRepository "0..1" o-[#D9652B,bold]- "0..*" ErrorLog : <color:#D9652B>Aggregation</color>\n<size:10>stores ▶ (log exists before it is saved)</size>

note right of RecordRepository
  <b>save()</b> = add or replace by log_id
  (same behaviour as old add_record).
  Converts with <i>log.to_dict()</i> and
  <i>ErrorLog.from_dict()</i>, so the JSON
  file format does not change.
  Missing / corrupt file → empty list.
end note

legend right
  <b>Legend</b>
  |= Concept |= Notation |
  | <color:#2F6DB5><b>Encapsulation</b></color> | <b>-</b> private, <b>+</b> public |
  | <color:#D9652B><b>Aggregation</b></color> | hollow ◇── at whole |
  |<back:#F4F4F4> grey dashed box </back>| class from another manager |
endlegend
@enduml
